{
  "id": "28929_kumon",
  "headword": "{苦悶|くもん}",
  "reading": "くもん",
  "romaji": "kumon",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "agony; anguish; deep suffering",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "agony; anguish; deep suffering",
      "explanation": "Intense physical or mental suffering — writhing in pain, or being torn by inner torment. A literary, fairly heavy word, common in novels, news reports, and medical descriptions."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28929_kumon_ex1",
      "japanese": "{苦悶|くもん}の{表情|ひょうじょう}を{浮|う}かべる。",
      "english": "To show a look of agony.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28929_kumon_ex2",
      "japanese": "{患者|かんじゃ}は{激|はげ}しい{腹痛|ふくつう}で{苦悶|くもん}していた。",
      "english": "The patient was writhing in agony from severe stomach pain.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28929_kumon_ex3",
      "japanese": "{長年|ながねん}の{心|こころ}の{苦悶|くもん}から{解放|かいほう}されて、ようやく{穏|おだ}やかな{気持|きも}ちになれた。",
      "english": "Released from years of inner anguish, I was finally able to feel at peace.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Compound of {苦|く} (suffering) + {悶|もん} (writhing in pain). Used as a noun and as a する verb ({苦悶|くもん}する). Implies severe, ongoing torment — not minor discomfort.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {苦悶|くもん}の{表情|ひょうじょう}: a look of agony\n- {苦悶|くもん}に{満|み}ちた{声|こえ}: a voice full of anguish\n- {苦悶|くもん}する: to writhe/agonize\n- {心|こころ}の{苦悶|くもん}: inner anguish\n- {苦悶|くもん}の{末|すえ}: after great anguish\n\nREGISTER:\nLiterary and heavy in tone. In casual speech, use {苦|くる}しむ or {悩|なや}む instead.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {苦痛|くつう}: pain; suffering — broader, can be mild or severe\n- {苦悩|くのう}: anguish; distress — emphasizes the mental/emotional side\n- {懊悩|おうのう}: deep mental anguish — even more literary",
